+# Movement plan (LONE-FLIP): 1 = a unit is not sent to flip an objective the
+# enemy holds when even the whole OC this plan puts there (our holders, units
+# en route, every unit the plan sends there, this unit) is below the OC the
+# enemy has standing on it NOW — the flip cannot happen even if the enemy never
+# moves — while the unit's own planner score for an objective where our models
+# already stand in a live fight (held under threat, contested, or the enemy
+# ahead by less than this unit's OC; within LONE_FLIP_MAX_TURNS) beats the flip
+# by LONE_FLIP_MIN_GAIN. It reinforces that objective instead (the same Move /
+# Advance the planner chose for it). Pass 1 counts a holder's whole OC though
+# only some of its models are in range, so that objective's need reads 0
+# ("already taken"): a 3-model Custodian Guard unit walked alone into a 14-OC
+# objective while the centre (ours 5 vs their 8 in range) was lost
+# (LLM-critic cluster lone_flip; Advancing to the centre measured +21.5 VP
+# [16.9, 26.1], 36 rollouts). That objective keeps paying every later round
+# (hold / centre primary rules, Centre Ground), so the unit is not held back.
+# 0 = previous behaviour.
+const FIX_LONE_FLIP: float = 1.0
+# LONE-FLIP: planner score points the reinforced objective must beat the flip by.
+const LONE_FLIP_MIN_GAIN: float = 10.0
+# LONE-FLIP: the reinforced objective must be reachable within this many moves.
+const LONE_FLIP_MAX_TURNS: int = 2
 # Charge (RETALIATION): share of the surviving target's melee damage on the
 # charger counted against the charge (x CHARGE_MELEE_DAMAGE_WEIGHT).
 const CHARGE_RETALIATION_WEIGHT: float = 0.5
